x86_64-linux  Two cxx1-only names, neither this case's subject. `_ZN4PolyC1Ev` is Poly's implicit constructor, an ordinary definition here and comdat linkonce_odr in clang's, which the collector does not see - the difference every .nonames in this directory with an implicit constructor records. `_ZN4VirtC2Ev` is Virt's base-object constructor, which clang emits only where a class derived from Virt constructs it as a base and this file never does; cxx1 emits C2 beside C1 for every class with a virtual base. Every member-pointer name - the four functions and the two callers - agrees.
arm64-darwin  `__ZN4VirtC2Ev` alone, the same base-object constructor.
x86_64-windows  One name each way, and they are one gap seen from both sides, the one own-vptr-plain-base.nonames and virtual-base-vbtable.nonames record: **the Microsoft RTTI for a non-polymorphic base under a polymorphic class**. clang emits `??_R17?0A@EA@Plain@@8`, a base-class descriptor for Plain in Poly's hierarchy, and cxx1 emits `??_R4Plain@@6B@`, a complete-object locator Plain has no use for. Nothing here reads either. The member-pointer names, the pair's shape and the adjustment are not in any name - the box's run of this case and tests/winlink/member-pointer-models measure them.
